Falsifies `system_tests::user::live_swap_tests::a_confined_client_drives_the_server_to_write_past_its_log`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect is the tree as it stood until the third outsider pass of milestone 633 (an outside agent attacks the confinement claim). The patch deletes the bound in `hot_swap_server::log_put`, so the
server writes a byte at `LOG_VA + log_base + arg` for any `arg` a client sends. A `WRITE`-only
client's `OPERATION_PUT` at `DEPUTY_PROBE` (`DEV_VA - LOG_VA`) then lands in the device register
page the server holds and the client does not, and the server answers as for an ordinary PUT.

Expected to fail: the `assert_ne!` whose message opens "CONFINEMENT ESCAPE: a WRITE-only client
made the swap server serve OPERATION_PUT at offset 0x100000". Replayed on 2026-10-06 (UTC) by the
milestone 633 lane: red at exactly that assertion on aarch64 (tag 0x100100000); green with the
bound on aarch64 and riscv64. x86_64 skips the test, having no device page.

diff --git a/crates/hot_swap_server/src/lib.rs b/crates/hot_swap_server/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/hot_swap_server/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/hot_swap_server/src/lib.rs
@@ -82,9 +82,6 @@
 /// `live_swap_tests::a_confined_client_drives_the_server_to_write_past_its_log`. Returns whether
 /// the byte was written.
 fn log_put(seq: u64, version: u64) -> bool {
-    if seq >= LOG_BYTES {
-        return false;
-    }
     // SAFETY: the log page is mapped read/write at LOG_VA in every process that calls this, and
     // `seq < LOG_BYTES` keeps the write inside that one page.
     unsafe { core::ptr::write_volatile((LOG_VA as *mut u8).add(seq as usize), version as u8) };
